Template: t-delayer-docker/network-mode
Type: select
Choices: host, bridge, existing
Default: host
Description: Docker network type for the delayer container:
 Host is recommended for multicast on a physical Linux network. Bridge is
 suitable for UI tests and multicast between containers on the same bridge.
 Existing uses a pre-created user-defined bridge, macvlan, or ipvlan network.
 PostgreSQL, delayer, and the UI run together in one container.

Template: t-delayer-docker/network-name
Type: string
Description: Existing Docker network name:
 Create this network before completing installation. Supported drivers are
 bridge, macvlan, and ipvlan. The package never removes this network.

Template: t-delayer-docker/container-ip
Type: string
Description: Static container IPv4 address (optional):
 Only used with an existing network. Leave empty for Docker IP allocation.
 The address must belong to the existing network and be reserved outside DHCP.

Template: t-delayer-docker/web-bind
Type: string
Default: 127.0.0.1
Description: Web UI bind address (web-bind):
 Enter 127.0.0.1 for access from this host only, 0.0.0.0 for all IPv4
 interfaces, or a specific local IPv4 address for one host interface.
 Host and bridge modes use this host address. The default is 127.0.0.1.
 With an existing macvlan or ipvlan network, this must be 0.0.0.0 and the UI
 is accessed directly at the container address. Use HTTPS for remote access.

Template: t-delayer-docker/web-port
Type: string
Default: 8080
Description: Web UI TCP port:
 Choose an unused port from 1 to 65535. The default is 8080.

Template: t-delayer-docker/multicast-interface
Type: string
Description: Local multicast interface IPv4 address (optional):
 Leave empty to use the routing table. In host mode, enter the host NIC's
 IPv4 address. With macvlan or ipvlan, enter the container's IPv4 address.
 Do not enter a multicast group or an interface name such as eth0.

Template: t-delayer-docker/video-path
Type: string
Default: /var/lib/t-delayer/video
Description: Absolute host directory for recorded video:
 Use a dedicated mounted disk for substantial recordings. The directory is
 mounted at /home/video in the container. Existing recordings are not moved
 when this setting changes. Database and login data stay in /var/lib/t-delayer.
